<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#LanguageVersion> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "btw"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "BeatScript 1: a text is in it when its header block has the version line #! btw 1, or no version line at all. Its canonical text has no #! line, and its program CID is the CID of the document {\"format\":1,\"text\":\"<canonical text>\",\"type\":\"djrust.live\"}."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote> "The name of the language before language version 2 was btw: BeatScript 1 is the language as it was written then. Every BeatScript 1 program, link and CID keeps its meaning; fmt upgrades a program to BeatScript 2, which plays the same under a new CID."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "BeatScript 1"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#programCidFormat> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#programCidType> "djrust.live" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#versionLine> "#! btw 1" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#versionOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-language> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#LanguageVersion> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "BeatScript 2: a text is in it when its header block has the version line #! beatscript 2. Its canonical text begins with #! beatscript 2, and its program CID is the CID of the document {\"format\":2,\"text\":\"<canonical text>\",\"type\":\"beatscript\"}. The current version: what fmt upgrades a program to and what the generators write."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "BeatScript 2"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasRevisionOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-1> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#programCidFormat> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#programCidType> "beatscript" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#versionLine> "#! beatscript 2" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/beatscript-2> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#versionOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-language> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_rhythm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The procedure that spreads K pulses over N steps as evenly as possible. Applied repeatedly, it merges the longer groups with the leftover shorter ones until at most one leftover remains."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Bjorklund algorithm"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/bjorklund> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A phrase answered by another phrase."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "call and response"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/call-and-response> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/camelot-wheel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/camelot-wheel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/camelot-wheel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A way of naming the twenty-four keys as numbers 1 to 12 with a letter, A for minor and B for major. Keys one step apart on the wheel, or at the same number with the other letter, mix harmonically."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/camelot-wheel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Camelot wheel"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/camelot-wheel> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/camelot-wheel> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/camelot-wheel> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A scale degree that belongs to the chord sounding now. Strong-beat melody notes are pulled to the nearest one."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "chord tone"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/chord-tone> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#Token> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The single token that moves around a ring, one step per tick. Its position is the playhead."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "circulating token"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/circulating-token> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The share of steps that sound rather than rest."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "density"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/density> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The section with no lines. Arranging it before or after any section leaves that section unchanged."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "empty section (identity)"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/empty-section-identity> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/empty-section-identity> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-end> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-end> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Ending> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-end> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The program stops when its last section finishes."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-end> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "end"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-end> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ending-end> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-end> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-loop> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-loop> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Ending> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-loop> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The program returns to its first section when its last finishes, and the net's marking resets to its initial marking."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-loop> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "loop"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-loop> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ending-loop> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/ending-loop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The pattern transforms, each taking a pattern to a pattern, closed under doing one after another, with doing nothing as the identity."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "endomorphism monoid"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/endomorphism-monoid> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EuclideanRhythm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A rhythm made by the Bjorklund algorithm. Many traditional patterns around the world are Euclidean rhythms. In the engine it becomes a rhythm ring with a note binding on each pulse step."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Euclidean rhythm"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/euclidean-rhythm> .
