<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/fmt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/fmt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/fmt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The formatter: rewrites a BeatScript program into its canonical form without changing what it plays. The fmt a person or an agent asks for also upgrades a BeatScript 1 program to BeatScript 2, a new CID for the same music; the formatting a program gets on its way in (eval, load, share, queue, push) keeps its version, so its CID never moves."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/fmt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "fmt"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/fmt> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/fmt> .
