<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-canon> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-canon> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Form> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-canon> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://beatscript.app/docs/forms#canon> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-canon> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The canon, a form from classical music: lead chase round sung round sung: one voice, then two, then three. The theme chases its own delayed and rotated copies; they are made of its bars, so `~ theme_* rot 2` and `rev` move the leader and its followers together."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-canon> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "canon"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-canon> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#formShape> "lead chase round sung round sung: one voice, then two, then three"@en .
