<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Form> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://beatscript.app/docs/forms#cross> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The cross, a form from classical music: a_leads b_leads both both sung a_leads b_leads sung: one source leads, then the other, then both at once. A quodlibet of two: `~ a_melody_* morph b_melody_1 p` paired with `~ b_bass_* morph a_bass_1 p`, an `@ ... xfer` one-shot in the overlap, then the pull turned round (`~ b_melody_* morph a_melody_1 p`, `~ a_bass_* morph b_bass_1 p`); `~` persists and compounds pass on pass (loop 3)."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "cross"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#formShape> "a_leads b_leads both both sung a_leads b_leads sung: one source leads, then the other, then both at once"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#formTemplate> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/template-cross> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-cross> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#mutationPlan> "a quodlibet of two: `~ a_melody_* morph b_melody_1 p` paired with `~ b_bass_* morph a_bass_1 p`, an `@ ... xfer` one-shot in the overlap, then the pull turned round (`~ b_melody_* morph a_melody_1 p`, `~ a_bass_* morph b_bass_1 p`); `~` persists and compounds pass on pass (loop 3)"@en .
