<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Form> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://beatscript.app/docs/forms#passacaglia> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The passacaglia, a form from classical music: ground variation sung variation sung variation sung: the ground under every section. Cumulative variations above the ground, each `~` added on top of the last: `rot 2 | accent`, `thin`, `rev | drift`, `grow`, `up 1`, `down 1`, `decay`; the ground is never mutated."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "passacaglia"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#formShape> "ground variation sung variation sung variation sung: the ground under every section"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#formTemplate> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/template-passacaglia> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/form-passacaglia> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#mutationPlan> "cumulative variations above the ground, each `~` added on top of the last: `rot 2 | accent`, `thin`, `rev | drift`, `grow`, `up 1`, `down 1`, `decay`; the ground is never mutated"@en .
