<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A melody made by a chain in which the next scale degree depends on the current one and the position in the bar: strong beats land on the nearest chord tone, weak beats move by step or repeat. A density setting then turns the weakest-beat notes into rests, never the first step."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Markov melody"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/markov-melody> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-accent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-accent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PatternModifier> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-accent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A term written c2! is accented: played louder than its neighbours."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-accent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "accent (!)"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-accent> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#markedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/keyword-symbol-bang> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-accent> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-accent> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#writtenAs> "!" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-chance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-chance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PatternModifier> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-chance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A term written x?p plays with probability p (0 to 1, or a percent), drawn from the program's seed so the same program always plays the same."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-chance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "chance (?p)"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-chance> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#markedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/keyword-symbol-question> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-chance> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-chance> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#writtenAs> "?" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-cycle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-cycle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PatternModifier> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-cycle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A part written hihat/12 has a cycle of n sixteenths instead of 16, so it drifts against the bar."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-cycle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "cycle length (/n)"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-cycle> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#markedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/keyword-symbol-slash> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-cycle> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-cycle> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#writtenAs> "/" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-repeat> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-repeat> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PatternModifier> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-repeat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A term written x*n plays n times in the time of one slot: hihat x*4 is four hits in one step."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-repeat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "repeat (*n)"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-repeat> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#markedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/keyword-symbol-star> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-repeat> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-repeat> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#writtenAs> "*" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-slide> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-slide> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PatternModifier> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-slide> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A term written e2^ slides into the next note instead of re-attacking, as on an acid bass line."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-slide> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "slide (^)"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-slide> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#markedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/keyword-symbol-caret> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-slide> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/modifier-slide> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#writtenAs> "^" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Stacking parts side by side: two parts played together make one part whose net is the disjoint union of the two. Written with the tensor sign. Associative and symmetric: the order parts are listed in does not change what plays."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "monoidal product"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/monoidal-product> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/monoidal-product> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-bass-swap> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-bass-swap> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-bass-swap> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Cut the outgoing deck's low end and bring in the incoming deck's, so two basslines never sound together."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-bass-swap> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "bass swap"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-bass-swap> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-bass-swap> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-bass-swap> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-echo-out> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-echo-out> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-echo-out> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Feed the outgoing deck into a delay and cut the dry signal, leaving the echoes to trail away."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-echo-out> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "echo out"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-echo-out> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-echo-out> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-echo-out> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-filter-exit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-filter-exit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-filter-exit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Close a filter on the outgoing deck until it fades out of the mix."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-filter-exit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "filter exit"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-filter-exit> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-filter-exit> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-filter-exit> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Repeat ever shorter slices of the playing audio to build tension."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "loop roll"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-loop-roll> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-loop-roll> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-phrase-sync> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-phrase-sync> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-phrase-sync> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Line the incoming deck up so its phrase starts on the outgoing deck's phrase boundary."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-phrase-sync> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "phrase sync"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-phrase-sync> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-phrase-sync> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-phrase-sync> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Pass the carrier role of a vocoder from one deck to the other so a voice carries across the change."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "vocoder handoff"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-every-nth-pass> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-every-nth-pass> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#LanguageTerm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-every-nth-pass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An arrange mutation written ~N target op (or @N target op) fires only on every Nth pass of its arrange block, on passes N, 2N, 3N and so on counted from 1; with no count it fires on every pass."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-every-nth-pass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "mutation count (~N, @N)"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-every-nth-pass> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#markedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/token-int> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-every-nth-pass> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-every-nth-pass> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#writtenAs> "~N" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-from-here> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-from-here> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#LanguageTerm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/mutation-from-here> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An arrange mutation written ~target op applies from that point of the arrangement to its end."@en .
