<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/themes-public-domain> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/themes-public-domain> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ThemeLibrary> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/themes-public-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://beatscript.app/themes> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/themes-public-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Melodies, basses and figures composed and first published before 1929, each written from the melody itself as BeatScript bars in a stated key, with its role, meter, source work, composer, year and pairings. A CC0 file, addressed by the CID of its text (beatscript.app/themes): the melodic twin of the phrasebook."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/themes-public-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "public-domain theme library"@en .
