<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-embed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-embed> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A program (or a set, or a station) embedded anywhere, from one embed config (https://beatscript.app/embed-config.schema.json, the same config the <beatscript-track> player and the <beatscript-studio> editor read): give a target and a config, and get the snippet or page for it, whether the config works there, is degraded or is unsupported, and one-sentence notes on what the target cannot do and what it does instead. Use the snippet as it is. Targets: artifact, web, iframe, oembed, preview, markdown, jupyter, vscode, obsidian, audio, rss, android, json. kind is player, studio (the whole editor as an MCP server inside the page: check, fmt, expand, generate, highlight, share, open, instruments, cheatsheet run offline on the wasm engine), card or audio; source is text, cid, set or station; audio is live, render, inline or url; features and capabilities are lists. With target artifact the answer is two text blocks, a JSON summary and the page: publish the page as an HTML page (an Artifact) exactly as it is, and declare the summary's capabilities (sample, mcp with the Beatscript connector's share, render and queue, db and user, downloads, room) when you publish it. Kind player or audio on target artifact is the artifact tool's page: kind audio (or audio inline) carries the site's render of a stored program in the page (a render not cached yet is limited as render's are), kind player plays it with the pinned player; kind studio loads @stackdump/beatscript-studio from cdn.jsdelivr.net at an exact version with Subresource Integrity. markdown (a GitHub README) gets an SVG card (https://beatscript.app/card/<CID>.svg) and an audio link; iframe, oembed, preview, audio, rss and obsidian need a program the site stores (share it signed in, or render it); android is the self-sealing /p# link the app opens. Give the program as text, cid or example (or in the config's source). No sign-in, and it stores nothing unless store (artifact, player or audio only); billed as a check. Text at most 16384 bytes. See https://beatscript.app/docs/embed."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-embed> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "embed"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-embed> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"cid\":{\"description\":\"CID of a program stored here, or of an example.\",\"maxLength\":100,\"pattern\":\"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{20,100}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"config\":{\"description\":\"The embed config (https://beatscript.app/embed-config.schema.json): kind, source, audio, features, capabilities, theme, compact, width, height, title, site, bridge, pin. Defaults by kind.\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"example\":{\"description\":\"Name of an example, from list_examples.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"store\":{\"description\":\"Target artifact, kind player or audio: store the text first (signed in), as the artifact tool does.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"target\":{\"description\":\"Where it goes. artifact (the default) gives a whole page.\",\"enum\":[\"artifact\",\"web\",\"iframe\",\"oembed\",\"preview\",\"markdown\",\"jupyter\",\"vscode\",\"obsidian\",\"audio\",\"rss\",\"android\",\"json\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text, instead of the config's source. It must pass check.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":{\"description\":\"The name to show and publish under (default the program's `#! name:`).\",\"maxLength\":80,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-embed> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
