<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Send a program to a browser tab that has https://beatscript.app open, as if the user pressed Cmd+Enter in the editor: the text replaces the editor's and the change lands on the next bar, with no gap; play:true starts playback too. Needs a bearer token.\n\nA tab must be connected. It is the page's own connection, so ask the user to open https://beatscript.app in a browser (signed in as the same account as the token, and eval reaches every live tab of that account), or, for a tab that is not signed in, to press MCP in the page's top bar and give you the session id it shows, which you pass as session. With no tab connected the answer is a no_session error that says this.\n\nRun check first. eval checks too and refuses a program with errors (nothing is sent; the diagnostics come back), and one that uses samples or \"use restricted\" (the browser has no such files). The program is the user's to hear: do not eval over something they are playing without saying so. After eval call get to see what is playing, the section and bar, and any diagnostics the page itself reports. The text is formatted on the way in, as fmt does (header lines and comments kept), so the editor shows it tidy. Text is at most 16384 bytes.\n\nLexicon harvest, a side effect with no flag: when the program checks and may be kept (no samples or loops, no `use restricted`, public visibility; push_private records nothing), the (word, phonemes) pairs of its lyrics are recorded to grow the CC0 lexicon: each annotated escape word=/phonemes/ (jingle=/j ii ng g uh l/ sings the escape and keeps the word) and each word no lexicon knows, with the rules' pronunciation. Only the word, its phonemes and the program's CID are kept, never the text. The answer's lexicon is {harvested, new}: the pairs taken from this program, and how many no program had given before. When check says a word is not in the lexicon and it sounds wrong, write it as word=/phonemes/."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "eval"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"device\":{\"description\":\"Id of one of your paired phones (djrust on Android), from the devices tool. Targets that phone alone; do not combine with session.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"play\":{\"description\":\"Start playing too (default false: load it and leave it stopped, or leave a playing tab as it is).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"session\":{\"description\":\"Session id of one browser tab, from the MCP panel of the page. Leave out to use your own signed-in tabs (every live one for eval/load/stop, the latest for get).\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text. It must pass check.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#requiredParameter> "text" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "eval" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "device" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "play" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "session" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-eval> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Play a program in a browser tab"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Write out every seed(...) and template(...) of a BeatScript program as the plain BeatScript it stands for, to start from a generated track and edit it. seed(genre, n[, structure]) is a track of the beats generator (genres: ambient blues bossa country dnb dubstep edm funk garage house jazz lofi metal reggae speedcore synthwave techno trance trap; structures: standard, loop, minimal, extended), and it is a value, never audio: `arrange from seed(techno, 42)` is the whole track, `section intro from seed(techno, 42)[1..8]` its first eight bars as a section, and `bass seed(techno, 42).bass[17..24]` (or `let riff = seed(techno, 42).bass[17..24]`) one part's bars as a pattern; seed@2(genre, n) is seeds v2, the same track with its genre's swing written (`arrange from seed@2(jazz, 7)` says swing 0.6; a bare seed(...) is seeds v1, written straight). template(name, phrase) compiles a phrase, a phrasebook id (@tempest_such_stuff) or any words in quotes, to a whole track, `arrange from template(deep-house, @tempest_such_stuff)` (templates: deep-house): the phrase is the vocal line, its syllables the line's length, its stress the accents and the beats, its meter the subdivision, and the arrangement is the template's own. A gen@N call (gen@2 techno seed=42 section=drop part=bass: the seeded generator, the program generate prints, pinned by its CID) is written out by where it stands: `arrange from gen@2 ...` as the whole program (under a `# from: gen@2 ... -> <cid>` line), a part line or `section X from gen@2 ... section=drop` as that section's parts, `let bed = gen@2 ... section=drop part=bass` as a let a bar (bed_1, bed_2, ..., bed = <bed_1 bed_2 ...>). check, eval and share take the references as they are and play the same music (the CID is of the short text); expand gives the long text, with a `# from seed(...)` or `# from template(...)` line over each place it wrote, to edit from there. Answers {ok, text, canonical, cid, from_cid, refs, resolution, diagnostics}: cid is the written-out program's, from_cid the one you gave; resolution is check's manifest (each reference once with its pin, and a template's nested parts, each with the CID of what it is written out as); with lineage true the text opens with `#! forked-from: <from_cid>`. With eject \"line:col\" it writes out only the reference there, in place, under its `# from: <call> -> <cid>` line (a comment: the ejected text has the CID of the same notes typed by hand), and answers {ok, text, cid, ejected: {call, kind, half, place, name, resolved, from}}. A `use SOURCE as NAME` line is written out as the definition its source makes (section NAME from ..., let NAME = ..., a theme's lets in the program's key), and a name in a role or a phrase's place as its source; the answer then also has imports, each name with its source. Read-only, no sign-in."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "expand"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"eject\":{\"description\":\"Optional: \\\"line:col\\\" (1-based) of one reference (a gen@N call, a seed(...), a <cid>.drop, a template(...)): eject it, writing just that one out in place under its `# from: <call> -> <cid>` line, the rest left as they are.\",\"maxLength\":16,\"pattern\":\"^[0-9]+:[0-9]+$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"lineage\":{\"description\":\"Open the written-out text with `#! forked-from: <CID of the program as given>` (default false), so that once it is shared it says what it came from.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text, with gen@N calls, seed(...) or template(...) references in it.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#requiredParameter> "text" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "expand" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "eject" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "lineage" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-expand> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Write out a program's seeds and templates"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Format a BeatScript program as the editor's fmt button does, in BeatScript 2: one statement a line, one space between tokens, blocks indented two spaces, numbers, notes and chords spelled one way, and the version line `#! beatscript 2` first; the other `#!` header lines, the comments and the blank lines between blocks stay where they are. A BeatScript 1 text (`#! btw 1`, or no version line) is upgraded: the same program under a new CID, and from_cid is the CID of the text as given (the old CID keeps working). Answers text (the formatted program), canonical (the same with no comments and no header lines but the version line: the CID is of that), cid, version (2), from_cid (only when it upgraded) and comments. A BeatScript 2 text formats to its own CID, so use fmt to tidy a program, to upgrade one, or to compare two; eval, load, queue, share and push_private already format what they are given and never upgrade it. A program that does not parse answers the same diagnostics as check. Read-only, no sign-in."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "fmt"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#requiredParameter> "text" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "fmt" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-fmt> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Format a BeatScript program"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-generate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-generate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Generate a whole BeatScript track from a seed, with no model and no sign-in: the beats generator picks the genre's rhythms (Euclidean), chord progression, instruments and song structure from the seed, and the result is printed as readable source (named lets, a def for the shared groove, sections, an arrange, filter ramps, the chords as Roman numerals and e()/arp()/markov()/every/rotate/degrade with their seeds written out, so one `key` line moves the whole song) for you to edit. Same genre, bpm, key, length and seed: the same text and CID, every time; the seed and generator are in the #! header so the track can be re-derived. The program passes check and is stored as public CC0 (source generate). Answers text, cid, name, seed, generator, url and render_url; play it with eval or load, or edit it and check again.\n\nThe answer also has gen, the call that is this program in BeatScript (gen@2 techno seed=42, with the bpm=, key= and length= you gave: `arrange from gen@2 techno seed=42` plays it), expanded_cid (the same as cid: a generated program has no references), and parts, so you can pick parts without reading the text: one entry a role, {role, section, sections, voice or kit, text, let, gen}, where gen is the call that is just that part (gen@2 techno seed=42 section=drop part=bass) and let is what `let drop_bass = <gen>` writes (a let a bar). Put a part's gen in a let or on a part line of your own program to layer it, mutate it in an arrange or cross it with another seed; there it is fitted to your program's key and tempo unless it says key= and bpm=, and check reports it in refs. With part (a role) the answer gains that part and its let alone; generator picks the version (1, 2, 3 or 4, as gen@1 to gen@4 name them; 3 writes BeatScript 2, 4 is 3 with the acid genre's bass on the 303); seeds (a list, or {count, start}, at most 16) answers a compact summary a seed instead of one program.\n\nLexicon harvest, a side effect with no flag: when the program checks and may be kept (no samples or loops, no `use restricted`, public visibility; push_private records nothing), the (word, phonemes) pairs of its lyrics are recorded to grow the CC0 lexicon: each annotated escape word=/phonemes/ (jingle=/j ii ng g uh l/ sings the escape and keeps the word) and each word no lexicon knows, with the rules' pronunciation. Only the word, its phonemes and the program's CID are kept, never the text. The answer's lexicon is {harvested, new}: the pairs taken from this program, and how many no program had given before. When check says a word is not in the lexicon and it sounds wrong, write it as word=/phonemes/."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-generate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "generate"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-generate> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"bpm\":{\"description\":\"Tempo; default the genre's.\",\"maximum\":300,\"minimum\":40,\"type\":\"number\"},\"ending\":{\"description\":\"How the song ends: end (default: after its last section) or loop (it starts again at its end). loop needs generator 3 or later.\",\"enum\":[\"end\",\"loop\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"generator\":{\"description\":\"The version of the seeded generator, as gen@N names it in a program: 1 (seeded@1, frozen), 2 (seeded@2, the chords and arps as Roman numerals), 3 (seeded@3: seeded@2's music written in BeatScript 2, `#! beatscript 2` first) or 4 (seeded@4: seeded@3 with the acid genre's bass on the 303, `inst=acid-bass`); default 4. A version always prints the same program for the same inputs.\",\"enum\":[1,2,3,4],\"type\":\"integer\"},\"genre\":{\"description\":\"The genre whose rhythms, chords, instruments and song structure it uses (default techno).\",\"enum\":[\"techno\",\"house\",\"jazz\",\"ambient\",\"dnb\",\"edm\",\"speedcore\",\"dubstep\",\"country\",\"blues\",\"synthwave\",\"trance\",\"lofi\",\"reggae\",\"funk\",\"bossa\",\"trap\",\"garage\",\"metal\",\"electro\",\"deephouse\",\"italo\",\"acid\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"key\":{\"description\":\"Key: am, c, f#m, d:dorian ...; default the genre's.\",\"maxLength\":16,\"type\":\"string\"},\"length\":{\"description\":\"Song length (default standard).\",\"enum\":[\"short\",\"standard\",\"long\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"part\":{\"description\":\"One part (a role): the answer gains part (that role's entry of parts) and let, the let its gen call writes (let drop_bass_1 = ... let drop_bass = <drop_bass_1 ...>), to paste into a program of your own.\",\"enum\":[\"kick\",\"snare\",\"hihat\",\"clap\",\"bass\",\"melody\",\"harmony\",\"arp\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"section\":{\"description\":\"With part: the section the part is taken from (default the drop or chorus when it plays there, else the first section it plays in).\",\"maxLength\":32,\"type\":\"string\"},\"seed\":{\"description\":\"A number or a word (default 1). Same inputs, same program text and CID.\",\"type\":[\"string\",\"integer\"]},\"seeds\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"items\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"integer\"]},\"maxItems\":16,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"count\":{\"maximum\":16,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"start\":{\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"count\"],\"type\":\"object\"}],\"description\":\"Instead of seed: many seeds, as a list ([1, 2, \\\"sunrise\\\"]) or as {count, start} (count seeds from start, default 1), at most 16. The answer is programs, one compact summary a seed in order: seed, generator, cid, name, key, tempo, bars, gen, parts (role, section, sections, voice or kit, text, gen) and url and render_url; each program is stored as one generate stores it, and nothing else is. The same seeds give the same summaries.\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-generate> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
