<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What a browser tab at https://beatscript.app is doing now, as the page last reported it: the program text and cid, playing (true/false), source (engine or stream), section (name), section_num of sections_total, bar, bars_in_section, phase (0-7, the light in the phrase), marks (what is firing: active lines, token flashes, ramps and timed lines, with line:col spans into the text), diagnostics (the page's own check of the text), ts, mixer (what the listener hears: crossfader, master, and per deck its level, mute, EQ kills, filter, insert filter and vocoder; null from a page or phone too old to report it) and warnings (a playing deck that cannot be heard, and why: \"deck B inaudible: the crossfader is all the way to A\"). Use it after eval or load to confirm the change landed, and to see the program a user is playing and editing.\n\nNeeds a bearer token: it reads the tabs of the token's account, by default the most recently seen one. A tab that is not signed in is read by its session id (the page's MCP panel shows it), with your token. Read-only. No tab connected: a no_session error that says how to connect one."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "get"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"device\":{\"description\":\"Id of one of your paired phones (djrust on Android), from the devices tool. Targets that phone alone; do not combine with session.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"session\":{\"description\":\"Session id of one browser tab, from the MCP panel of the page. Leave out to use your own signed-in tabs (every live one for eval/load/stop, the latest for get).\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "get" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "device" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "session" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-get> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "What a browser tab is playing"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sounds a program may name: voices (inst=NAME), families (a name that contains one plays that family's generic voice and check warns about it), drum kits (kit=NAME) and palettes. Use only names from this answer: an unknown inst= is a check error with the nearest names. acid (a saw) and acid-square are a 303-style voice made in the engine: an accent ! is louder and opens its filter further, accents in a row build, a slide ^ glides into the next note (60 ms, or glide=), decay= is its filter's decay. Read-only, no sign-in, cached for five minutes."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "instruments"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "instruments" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-instruments> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Voices, kits and palettes"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A stored program's family tree, from the rights each program keeps (forked_from): its ancestors (nearest first), its siblings (the parent's other forks) and every generation of its forks, each edge labelled with what changed in music from parent to fork (the same diff summary lines check's same_as gives: \"tempo 124 -> 126\", \"drop2 bass = drop bass transposed +1\"; sameSong true when the fork only rewrote the text). Returns the JSON-LD document https://beatscript.app/p/<CID>/tree.jsonld serves: program, forkCount, descendantCount, ancestors, siblings and forks as CIDs, programs (name, licence, tempo, key, credits, url, forkCount of each, and where public programs draw on it, referencedBy: how many call or borrow it, and vendoredFrom: how many vendored it, from the `# from:` lines their saves kept as meta.based_on), derivations (from, to, sameSong, change, and a compare URL, https://beatscript.app/p/<A>/compare/<B>). Only public programs appear: a private one is never listed, and a chain that passes through one stops there (ancestorsCut). A person can browse the same tree at https://beatscript.app/p/<CID>/tree."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "lineage"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"cid\":{\"description\":\"The program: its CID, or a short https://beatscript.app/p/<CID> link. It must be stored here (or be an example) and public.\",\"maxLength\":200,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"cid\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#requiredParameter> "cid" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "lineage" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-lineage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "A program's family tree"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-list-examples> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-list-examples> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The public example programs of https://beatscript.app, all CC0-1.0: name, title, description, cid, bpm, bars, license and the url of the raw .beatscript. Pass name to get that program's full text as well. Read two or three before writing a program of your own: after the cheat-sheet (https://beatscript.app/docs/cheatsheet.md) they are the best guide to the language, from a four-line beat (first-beat) to whole tracks with sections, defs, ramps and evolve. With phrasebook true (or a meter, or syllables) it also returns the public-domain phrasebook: lines first published before 1929, each with its text, source, year, meter, stress pattern, syllables and phoneme escapes, to sing by id (sing @tempest_such_stuff on melody); choose one for its meter, see https://beatscript.app/docs/found-phrases.md. With themes true (or a key, a role or a composer) it also returns the public-domain theme library: melodies, basses and figures composed and published before 1929, each as BeatScript bars in a stated key with the let lines and the part that play it, its work, composer, year and the themes it morphs well with; borrow one as found material or build a form from it, see https://beatscript.app/docs/forms.md. With imports true it also lists what a `use SOURCE as NAME` line can name: the kinds of source, each template's sections (use template(passacaglia).ground as ground) and each genre template's (use genre@1 techno.drop as drop), see https://beatscript.app/docs/BEATSCRIPT.md \"Name a source: `use`\". Read-only, no sign-in."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-list-examples> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "list_examples"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-list-examples> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"composer\":{\"description\":\"Only the themes by this composer (any part of the name: beethoven). Implies themes.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"type\":\"string\"},\"imports\":{\"description\":\"Also return what a `use SOURCE as NAME` line can name (default false): the kinds of source, each with how it is written and what the name is; the templates and their sections (canned sections: use template(passacaglia).ground as ground); the genre templates and their sections (use genre@1 techno.drop as drop); themes and phrasebook lines are listed by themes and phrasebook.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"key\":{\"description\":\"Only the themes in this key, matched on its tonic: a key word (d, bm, db). Implies themes.\",\"maxLength\":16,\"type\":\"string\"},\"lexicon\":{\"description\":\"Also return the lexicon harvest (default false): the words the checking tools collected from programs' lyrics, ranked for the CC0 lexicon, at most 50: those with an annotated escape (word=/phonemes/) first, then by how many programs gave them. Each is {word, programs, conflict, in_lexicon, variants[{phones, source (annotated or rule), count, first, last, cids}]}; conflict: two annotated pronunciations disagree. Read-only.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"meter\":{\"description\":\"Only the phrasebook lines of this meter: a family (iambic, trochaic, anapestic, dactylic, common-meter, sprung, nursery, parallelism, oratory, call-and-response) or a word of a meter's name (pentameter). Implies phrasebook.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"Optional: also return this example's full text.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"phrasebook\":{\"description\":\"Also return the public-domain phrasebook: lines first published before 1929, each with its text, source, year, meter, stress pattern, syllables and phoneme escapes (default false).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"role\":{\"description\":\"Only the themes of this role: melody, bass, harmony or arp. Implies themes.\",\"maxLength\":16,\"type\":\"string\"},\"syllables\":{\"description\":\"Only the phrasebook lines with this many syllables: a number (8) or a range (8-12). Implies phrasebook.\",\"maxLength\":16,\"type\":\"string\"},\"themes\":{\"description\":\"Also return the public-domain theme library: melodies, basses and figures composed and published before 1929, each as BeatScript bars in a stated key (let-ready), with its role, meter, work, composer, year and pairings (default false).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
