<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-listen> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-listen> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Listen to a BeatScript program without audio: it is rendered offline through the same engine as render, and you get a small JSON summary to check your work by ear, as numbers. Per deck and per part (a role of a deck's line: drums, bass, ...): RMS and peak in dBFS and loudness in LUFS. `silent` lists every deck or part that has notes in the window but is not heard (under -60 LUFS), with `reason` when the mixer explains it (master_zero, mute, level_0, crossfader, filter_closed, eq_killed; voice_missing when the mixer lets a part through and its voice made nothing; no_sound otherwise) and `why` in words. `detected` gives the tempo and key heard against the declared ones (bpm_match same|half|double|two_thirds|three_halves|differs; key_match same|relative|differs|unsure|undeclared). `sections` gives each section's loudness (and `control_off` on a section an `arrange { }` switch such as `~ control off` plays with lines of its control deck held back: the calls that do not fire there), `bar_lufs` a loudness per bar, and master.clipped_samples counts samples over full scale. `warnings` is the short list to act on. A part that came from a reference (a gen@2 call, a seed(...), a template, a stored program's section) says so in `from` {call, kind, resolved, place, generator, sections} (`also_from` when several made it; a `use` line's also has its `name`); a gen call fitted to the program's key or tempo says so in `notes`, in check's words; and the answer gains `expanded_cid` and `resolution`, as check's (and `imports`, the names its `use` lines give). Give exactly one of text, cid, example; optionally `section` (listen to that section only) and `bars` (at most this many bars of the window). Nothing is stored and no sign-in is needed. At most 30 new listens an hour per caller; the same program, section and bars again is answered from the cache. Programs are at most 16384 bytes; the render covers at most 96 bars from the start. Like render, the offline engine plays the program as the browser's engine does (its control lines too: the mixer, inserts and their ramps, the vocoder, the Wheel, moves, kit= and sound=) and the `macro` lines (the DJ macro catalogue: see the macros tool); `notes` names any control line it leaves out. A program with a macro line gains `macros`: each call in the window, `at_bar` (the bar the engine starts it on, as the time words count), and `played`, with `refused` (the engine's reason, also a warning) when it was not. The mix, to polish it by ear: each measured part and the master have `bands` (dB in sub 20-60 Hz, low 60-250, low_mid 250-500, mid 500-2k, high_mid 2k-6k, high 6k up, on rms_db's scale), `centroid_hz`, `width` (0 mono, 0.5 wide, 1 out of phase), `correlation` and `crest_db`; the master also `true_peak_db` (dBTP, 4x oversampled), `plr_db`, `short_term_max_lufs` and `lra`; each section its `bands` and `true_peak_db`. `clashes` lists parts that carry the same band in the same bars at levels that mask each other ({parts, band, hz, bars, overlap, gap_db, sections}, the louder part first). `targets` (default streaming: -14 LUFS, -1 dBTP; also apple, broadcast, club, or LUFS/dBTP such as -12/-1) gives the master's lufs_delta and true_peak_delta and `met`. `warnings` come in the order to fix them (not heard, clipping, clashes, balance, loudness, width), each saying the BeatScript line that fixes it, and `warning_ids` gives each a stable id. With `compare` (the previous version: a CID or its text) the answer gains `compare`: deltas (now minus before) of the master, each part and each section, the targets before and after, and the warnings `fixed`, `introduced` and `kept`, with a one-line `summary`. On a long program listen a `section` at a time: a part past the budget of part renders is not measured (notes says so) and has no bands. The loop (check, listen, edit, listen with compare) and which lines fix what: https://beatscript.app/docs/polish.md.\n\nLexicon harvest, a side effect with no flag: when the program checks and may be kept (no samples or loops, no `use restricted`, public visibility; push_private records nothing), the (word, phonemes) pairs of its lyrics are recorded to grow the CC0 lexicon: each annotated escape word=/phonemes/ (jingle=/j ii ng g uh l/ sings the escape and keeps the word) and each word no lexicon knows, with the rules' pronunciation. Only the word, its phonemes and the program's CID are kept, never the text. The answer's lexicon is {harvested, new}: the pairs taken from this program, and how many no program had given before. When check says a word is not in the lexicon and it sounds wrong, write it as word=/phonemes/."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-listen> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "listen"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-listen> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"bars\":{\"description\":\"At most this many bars of the window, from its start.\",\"maximum\":96,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"cid\":{\"description\":\"CID of a stored program or an example.\",\"maxLength\":100,\"pattern\":\"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{20,100}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"compare\":{\"description\":\"The previous version to compare with: a CID or the program's text. The answer gains `compare` (what changed, and the warnings fixed and introduced); the same section, bars and targets are used for both.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"},\"example\":{\"description\":\"Name of an example, from list_examples.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"section\":{\"description\":\"Listen to this section only (its name in the program).\",\"maxLength\":64,\"type\":\"string\"},\"targets\":{\"description\":\"The delivery target the master is measured against: streaming (default: -14 LUFS, -1 dBTP), apple (-16, -1), broadcast (-23, -1), club (-8, -0.3), or LUFS/dBTP such as -12/-1.\",\"maxLength\":32,\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text. It must pass check. Not stored.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-listen> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
