<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-load> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-load> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Put a stored or example program into a browser tab (the same tabs and rules as eval: a tab open at https://beatscript.app, signed in as the token's account, or its session id from the page's MCP panel). Give exactly one of: cid (a program the site stored, or an example's CID; render and a signed-in share store theirs), example (a name from list_examples), url (a share link https://beatscript.app/#CID.packed or a /c/ link; one made on an older host opens too; the link is verified, and one whose CID is not its text's is refused with cid_mismatch). play:true starts it. The program is formatted on the way in, as eval's text is. Needs a bearer token. Call get afterwards to see what is playing.\n\nLexicon harvest, a side effect with no flag: when the program checks and may be kept (no samples or loops, no `use restricted`, public visibility; push_private records nothing), the (word, phonemes) pairs of its lyrics are recorded to grow the CC0 lexicon: each annotated escape word=/phonemes/ (jingle=/j ii ng g uh l/ sings the escape and keeps the word) and each word no lexicon knows, with the rules' pronunciation. Only the word, its phonemes and the program's CID are kept, never the text. The answer's lexicon is {harvested, new}: the pairs taken from this program, and how many no program had given before. When check says a word is not in the lexicon and it sounds wrong, write it as word=/phonemes/."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-load> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "load"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-load> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"cid\":{\"description\":\"CID of a program the site has stored (render and a signed-in share store theirs) or of an example.\",\"maxLength\":100,\"pattern\":\"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{20,100}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"device\":{\"description\":\"Id of one of your paired phones (djrust on Android), from the devices tool. Targets that phone alone; do not combine with session.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"example\":{\"description\":\"Name of an example, from list_examples.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"play\":{\"description\":\"Start playing too (default false: load it and leave it stopped, or leave a playing tab as it is).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"session\":{\"description\":\"Session id of one browser tab, from the MCP panel of the page. Leave out to use your own signed-in tabs (every live one for eval/load/stop, the latest for get).\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"url\":{\"description\":\"A share link: https://beatscript.app/#<CID>.<packed>, a /c/ link, or a short /p/<CID> link (one made on an older host opens too) (the program must be stored here).\",\"maxLength\":32768,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-load> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
