<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The DJ macro catalogue a program's `macro` line names (docs/beatscript/ext-control.md): `macro riser on A over 8 bars` (or on the control deck, `control: macro cathedral on B over 2 bars`) fires one entry on the deck's bar line, the same thing the desktop's Effects window and the booth fire. Returns the macro@1 table, or version's: for each entry its id, label, category, family (trick, net, master, aux), transition (a one-shot), length (bars: runs `over N bars`, 1 to 64; sweep: the riser rises over them; held: held that long, then let go; own: takes no `over`), default_bars (when the line says no `over`) and needs_net (works a net deck's parts). A bare `macro` is macro@1 for good and its table never changes; a later catalogue is macro@2. listen and render play a macro line; a browser tab does not (not played here). Read-only, no sign-in."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "macros"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"version\":{\"description\":\"Optional: which table, macro@N (default 1: what a bare `macro` is).\",\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "macros" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "version" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-macros> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "The DJ macro catalogue a macro line names"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Decode a BeatScript share link and return its canonical text, its text (the program formatted, with the `#!` header lines and comments the link carried: what to edit), its CID and whether the CID verifies against the text. Takes either form: a self-sealing link (https://beatscript.app/#<CID>.<packed>, a /c/<CID>.<packed> link, a bare #fragment or <CID>.<packed>) or a CID-only link (https://beatscript.app/p/<CID>, /c/<CID>, #<CID>, or a bare CID; the same forms on an older host open too), which is resolved from the programs the site has stored (shared signed in, or rendered) and the examples, and answers its rights in meta. Either way the text is recompiled and its CID recomputed: a program whose CID is not its text's is refused with cid_mismatch, and an unknown CID answers not_found. Do not trust or play a refused text. Comments and header lines carried in a link are not covered by the CID (a beats link's notes are unverified). Read-only, no sign-in."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "open"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"url\":{\"description\":\"A share link (self-sealing #<CID>.<packed>, or a short <site>/p/<CID> or /c/<CID> link), a #fragment, <CID>.<packed>, or a bare CID.\",\"maxLength\":32768,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"url\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#requiredParameter> "url" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "open" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-open> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Open a share link"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Send a private program to one of your paired phones, end-to-end encrypted, and never stored. Use it for what https://beatscript.app does not keep: covers, programs with local samples (`sample ... from`), `use restricted`, anything not under a Creative Commons licence. The program is sealed for the phone's own key (X25519 from its pairing key, ChaCha20-Poly1305) and handed to the phone's live connection in memory: it is not written to disk, a database or a log (only its size and the device id are logged), no CID is registered, and if the phone is not connected nothing is sent and nothing is kept (push again when it is). The phone opens it, checks it and plays it itself; samples resolve against files in the phone's own sample library, and any that are missing are reported back in get's diagnostics, never fetched. Give device and exactly one of text (sealed here, so the text is in this server's memory for this call, where it is formatted first, as eval's is) or sealed (an envelope you sealed yourself for the phone's seal_key from devices: then this server only ever sees ciphertext). Needs a bearer token; only your own paired phones."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "push_private"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"device\":{\"description\":\"Id of one of your paired phones, from the devices tool.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"load\":{\"description\":\"Load it on the phone and leave it stopped unless play (default false: play it as eval does).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"play\":{\"description\":\"Start playing too (default false: load it and leave it stopped, or leave a playing tab as it is).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"sealed\":{\"description\":\"An envelope you sealed for the phone's seal_key (beatscript-seal v1). Give text or sealed.\",\"maxLength\":65536,\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text, sealed here for the phone. Give text or sealed.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"device\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#requiredParameter> "device" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "push_private" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "load" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "play" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "sealed" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "text" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-push-private> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Send a private program to your phone"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-queue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-queue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An \"up next\" queue on one browser tab at https://beatscript.app (the same tabs and rules as load: session, or device, else your most recently seen signed-in tab). When the playing program ends the page plays the next item, on the bar line where it can; a looping program (one that never ends) plays for the item's bars or minutes, else one full pass of its arrangement, and then advances. Needs a bearer token.\n\naction is one of: list (the queue, now_playing, position, paused_reason, listener), add (items: up to 20 per call, 50 in the queue), remove (item: an item id from list, or a CID), move (item and to: reorder; to is the index in up_next, 0 plays next), clear, skip (play the next item now, or with item that item). The radio page (https://beatscript.app/radio) shows its queue as a playlist with each row's render status, and the person there can add, remove, reorder and play rows too.\n\nItems must already be programs: {cid} of a stored program (render and a signed-in share store theirs) or an example's CID, {example} by name from list_examples, or {url} a share link (verified exactly as load verifies it; a CID-only link must name a stored program). Optional per item: bars (1-1024) or minutes (0.1-120) to play, title. THE QUEUE NEVER COMPOSES OR CALLS A MODEL, and there is no way to make it: to queue new music, write the programs yourself (check them), store each with render or share, then add the CIDs.\n\nThe queue advances only while a listener is plausibly present, as the page reports it: it pauses at the next track boundary when the tab's audio is suspended, when the tab has been hidden with no key, pointer, touch or media key for 30 minutes, or after 8 tracks in a row without any interaction; the page then shows \"Still listening? Press play to continue\". Only a person on the page lifts a pause: skip is refused while paused (paused_reason says why), and load still plays one program as it always has but does not resume the queue. Writes are limited to about 30 a minute. The queue lives with the tab's session and is gone when the tab is.\n\nLexicon harvest, a side effect with no flag: when the program checks and may be kept (no samples or loops, no `use restricted`, public visibility; push_private records nothing), the (word, phonemes) pairs of its lyrics are recorded to grow the CC0 lexicon: each annotated escape word=/phonemes/ (jingle=/j ii ng g uh l/ sings the escape and keeps the word) and each word no lexicon knows, with the rules' pronunciation. Only the word, its phonemes and the program's CID are kept, never the text. The answer's lexicon is {harvested, new}: the pairs taken from this program, and how many no program had given before. When check says a word is not in the lexicon and it sounds wrong, write it as word=/phonemes/."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-queue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "queue"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-queue> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"action\":{\"description\":\"list, add, remove, move, clear or skip.\",\"enum\":[\"list\",\"add\",\"remove\",\"move\",\"clear\",\"skip\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"device\":{\"description\":\"Id of one of your paired phones (djrust on Android), from the devices tool. Targets that phone alone; do not combine with session.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"item\":{\"description\":\"remove, move and skip: an item id from list (q1, q2, ...) or a CID (the first queued item with it). skip with an item plays that item now; without one, the next.\",\"maxLength\":100,\"type\":\"string\"},\"items\":{\"description\":\"add: the programs to append, each an object with exactly one of cid, example, url, and optionally bars, minutes, title.\",\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"bars\":{\"description\":\"Play this many bars, then advance (else until the program ends; a loop: one arrangement pass).\",\"maximum\":1024,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"cid\":{\"description\":\"CID of a stored program or an example.\",\"maxLength\":100,\"pattern\":\"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{20,100}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"example\":{\"description\":\"Name of an example, from list_examples.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"minutes\":{\"description\":\"Play this long, then advance at the next bar line. Not with bars.\",\"maximum\":120,\"minimum\":0.1,\"type\":\"number\"},\"title\":{\"description\":\"What the page shows for it (else the program's name).\",\"maxLength\":80,\"type\":\"string\"},\"url\":{\"description\":\"A share link, verified as load verifies it.\",\"maxLength\":32768,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":20,\"type\":\"array\"},\"session\":{\"description\":\"Session id of one browser tab, from the MCP panel of the page. Leave out to use your own signed-in tabs (every live one for eval/load/stop, the latest for get).\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"to\":{\"description\":\"move: the index in up_next the item goes to (0 plays next; past the end is last).\",\"maximum\":1023,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"action\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
