<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-queue> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Up next: queue programs on a browser tab"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Set up a demo recording of a program: the page in record mode (full screen code, the firing markers and follow-scroll on) and the steps that turn it into a video. Give exactly one of text, cid or example (as render does: a text or example is checked and stored publicly as CC0-1.0, nothing private). Answers {cid, seconds, record_url, record_url_manual_clock, audio_url, recipe}. record_url opens the page in record mode and plays it for a person to screen-record; record_url_manual_clock opens it on a fake clock that a script steps frame by frame (window.__btw.setTime(seconds); window.__btw.frame()), which is how site/tools/record-demo.mjs in the repo makes a perfectly synced, stutter-free MP4 (H.264, AAC, 1920x1080) plus a silent hero loop (MP4 and WebM) and a poster PNG, taking the audio from audio_url (the offline render of the same program). This tool does not capture video itself: it needs a browser and ffmpeg on your side. The audio is the offline render: notes and sounds, not control lines (filters, reverb). Call check first. Rendering limits apply (about 30 programs an hour per client). No sign-in needed."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "record"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"cid\":{\"description\":\"CID of a program already stored (for instance the cid render or a signed-in share returned).\",\"maxLength\":100,\"pattern\":\"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{20,100}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"example\":{\"description\":\"Name of an example, from list_examples.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text. It must pass check; it is stored publicly (CC0-1.0).\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "record" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "cid" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "example" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "text" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-record> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Set up a demo recording"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Make a program streamable as audio. Give exactly one of text (the program), cid (a program already stored, e.g. what an earlier render or a signed-in share returned) or example (a name from list_examples). A text or example is checked, then stored publicly under its CID as CC0-1.0 if it is not stored yet (never submit anything private; programs that use samples or \"use restricted\" are refused). Answers {cid, stream_url, status_url, seconds, format}: open stream_url to listen (it streams the offline render as it renders; the first sound comes within about a second, so a client can play it at once), download the same URL for a file, and read status_url to see how far a render is. format is opus (Ogg Opus, small) or wav (16-bit stereo, plays chunk by chunk in a web page); default opus. To take the program to a DAW: format midi (a Standard MIDI File: a track per part, drums on channel 10 with General MIDI notes, the tempo map, key and section markers) or stems (a zip of a 32-bit float WAV per part and per deck that add up to the master, plus the master, the .mid and manifest.json with the CID, tempo, key and the stored license and credits; stems-opus: the same with Ogg Opus stems; stems-dry and stems-dry-opus: dry stems, each part before its deck and the master, with the control moves they leave out in manifest.json); a stems URL answers 202 while it is being made, ask again until it is the zip.\n\nCall check first. The offline render plays the program as the browser's engine does, on the same engine code: the notes and sounds (kit= and sound= too) and the control lines (filters and resonance, reverb, levels, EQ, the crossfader, their ramps and lfos, the vocoder, the Wheel, moves, section and timed lines), and also what the page does not play yet (delay, crush on a deck, macro lines, duck); its notes name any line it leaves out. A program with no end (no sections or end line) is cut at the server's bar limit (256 bars). Rendering is limited per address per hour and to a few at once: on busy or rate_limited wait retry_after seconds. No sign-in needed; about 30 programs an hour per client.\n\nLexicon harvest, a side effect with no flag: when the program checks and may be kept (no samples or loops, no `use restricted`, public visibility; push_private records nothing), the (word, phonemes) pairs of its lyrics are recorded to grow the CC0 lexicon: each annotated escape word=/phonemes/ (jingle=/j ii ng g uh l/ sings the escape and keeps the word) and each word no lexicon knows, with the rules' pronunciation. Only the word, its phonemes and the program's CID are kept, never the text. The answer's lexicon is {harvested, new}: the pairs taken from this program, and how many no program had given before. When check says a word is not in the lexicon and it sounds wrong, write it as word=/phonemes/."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "render"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"cid\":{\"description\":\"CID of a program already stored (for instance the cid render or a signed-in share returned).\",\"maxLength\":100,\"pattern\":\"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{20,100}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"example\":{\"description\":\"Name of an example, from list_examples.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"format\":{\"default\":\"opus\",\"description\":\"opus (Ogg Opus, smaller, for download or <audio>) or wav (16-bit stereo, plays chunk by chunk in a web page) to listen; for a DAW: midi (a Standard MIDI File of the notes, a track per part), stems (a zip: a 32-bit float WAV per part and per deck that add up to the master, the master, the .mid and manifest.json with the CID, tempo, key, license and credits) or stems-opus (the same zip with Ogg Opus stems); stems-dry and stems-dry-opus: dry stems (each part before its deck and the master: no level, crossfader, EQ, filter, sends or master effects), with every control move they leave out, and the master's effects, in manifest.json.\",\"enum\":[\"opus\",\"wav\",\"midi\",\"stems\",\"stems-opus\",\"stems-dry\",\"stems-dry-opus\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text. It must pass check; it is stored publicly (CC0-1.0).\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "render" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "cid" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "example" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "format" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "text" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-render> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Render a program to streaming audio"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-share> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-share> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Make the share links of a program. Always the self-sealing link: https://beatscript.app/#<CID>.<base64url(deflate(formatted text))>; the program travels inside the link with its `#!` header lines and comments, and whoever opens it gets exactly that program, verified against the CID (the canonical text's: the headers and comments are not covered by it), and can play and fork it. Also social_url (https://beatscript.app/c/<CID>.<packed>, the form to post where a link preview is wanted: it carries a card image). Called signed in (a bearer token), it also stores the program on the site (public, with its rights: license, forked_from, credits, name; the first share's rights stay) and returns the CID-only forms: short_url (https://beatscript.app/p/<CID>) and short_social_url (https://beatscript.app/c/<CID>), plus fetch_url, a public GET that returns the canonical text and rights for a phone or an app. A program with references (a template(...), a gen@N call, a seed(...), a borrowed <cid>.section) has expanded_cid, the CID of the same track with every reference written out as plain BeatScript; a signed-in share stores that expansion beside it, as a program of its own that plays the same (or finds it already stored: first write wins, so it keeps the rights its first sharer gave), and returns expanded_url (https://beatscript.app/p/<expanded_cid>) and expansion_license. An expansion that would copy another's program under other rights (only CC0 programs, or the sharer's own under the same licence, are copied), or is over the size limit, is not stored, and expansion_note says why. Opening a short link fetches the text, recompiles it, recomputes the CID and refuses a mismatch. A short link to a BeatScript 1 program (https://beatscript.app/p/<old CID>) redirects to its BeatScript 2 upgrade (the CID check's renamed_cid gives, the program fmt writes) once the site stores it; the old CID's text stays at fetch_url. Anonymous calls get the self-sealing links and short_url null. The program must pass check and must not use samples or \"use restricted\" (a private program is never shared or stored); programs shared here are CC0 unless license says otherwise. The text is formatted on the way in, its version kept (the stored program is its canonical text, whose CID the header lines and comments do not change, and the link carries the formatted text; a `#! name:` line names the stored program). Its `# from: <call> -> <cid>` lines (what an eject wrote out: comments, so not in the CID) are kept with it as meta.based_on [\"<call> -> <cid>\"]: its linked data lists each in isBasedOn as vendored, and lineage counts it (vendoredFrom); open with the CID answers them in meta. Links over about 2000 characters (chars says) may be cut by some apps; short links are not. A stored program also embeds in other sites: embed_url (https://beatscript.app/embed/<CID>) is a player any page may frame, https://beatscript.app/embed.js gives <beatscript-player cid=\"<CID>\">, and https://beatscript.app/oembed?url=<a /p/ or /c/ link> answers oEmbed; see https://beatscript.app/docs/embed. Who authored a program and what rights it has, in plain language: https://beatscript.app/authorship.\n\nLexicon harvest, a side effect with no flag: when the program checks and may be kept (no samples or loops, no `use restricted`, public visibility; push_private records nothing), the (word, phonemes) pairs of its lyrics are recorded to grow the CC0 lexicon: each annotated escape word=/phonemes/ (jingle=/j ii ng g uh l/ sings the escape and keeps the word) and each word no lexicon knows, with the rules' pronunciation. Only the word, its phonemes and the program's CID are kept, never the text. The answer's lexicon is {harvested, new}: the pairs taken from this program, and how many no program had given before. When check says a word is not in the lexicon and it sounds wrong, write it as word=/phonemes/."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-share> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "share"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-share> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"credits\":{\"description\":\"Who is credited, one short line each. Stored with the rights.\",\"items\":{\"maxLength\":80,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":8,\"type\":\"array\"},\"forked_from\":{\"description\":\"CID of the program this one was forked from. Stored with the rights.\",\"maxLength\":100,\"pattern\":\"^z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{20,100}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"license\":{\"description\":\"Rights kept with the stored program: a Creative Commons SPDX id (default CC0-1.0; CC-BY-4.0, CC-BY-SA-4.0 and the like). The site stores no other licence: keep such a program local, or send it to your phone with push_private.\",\"maxLength\":40,\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"A name for the program (else its `#! name:` line).\",\"maxLength\":80,\"type\":\"string\"},\"text\":{\"description\":\"The program text. It must pass check.\",\"maxLength\":16384,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-share> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-share> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
