<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Stop what a browser tab at https://beatscript.app is playing: the program ends and whatever its lines held (a filter, a mute) is put back. Reaches every live tab of the token's account, or one tab by session (the id the page's MCP panel shows). Needs a bearer token. No tab connected: a no_session error that says how to connect one."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "stop"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"device\":{\"description\":\"Id of one of your paired phones (djrust on Android), from the devices tool. Targets that phone alone; do not combine with session.\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"session\":{\"description\":\"Session id of one browser tab, from the MCP panel of the page. Leave out to use your own signed-in tabs (every live one for eval/load/stop, the latest for get).\",\"maxLength\":64,\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{6,64}$\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "stop" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "device" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "session" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-beatscript-stop> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolTitle> "Stop a browser tab"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Everything the ontology states about one class, property, genre, scale, groove, section, instrument or concept, as N-Triples (the materialized graph). Give a short name such as Genre, bpm, genre:techno or section:drop, or a full IRI in the ontology's namespaces. format \"json\" returns a compact view instead: label, types, definition (its own, else the glossary concept it closeMatches, else its rdfs:comment), direct superclasses and subclasses as asserted, close matches and sources."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "describe_term"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#inputSchema> "{\"properties\":{\"format\":{\"description\":\"triples (default, N-Triples) or json (compact term view)\",\"enum\":[\"triples\",\"json\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"term\":{\"description\":\"name or IRI\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"term\"],\"type\":\"object\"}" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#needsToken> "false"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#providedBy> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/product-beatscript-ontology-mcp> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#readOnly> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#requiredParameter> "term" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolName> "describe_term" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-describe-term> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#toolParameter> "format" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-get-genre> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#McpTool> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-get-genre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One genre in full: tempo, scale, kick/snare/hihat Euclidean rhythms (pulses, steps, rotation, MIDI note), swing, humanize, densities, instrument per channel, chord progressions, song-structure sections, and links to Wikidata and to pflow ontology terms. Give a slug such as techno or jazz."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/concept/tool-ontology-get-genre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "get_genre"@en .
