<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The normal form of a BeatScript program: whitespace, numbers, note spelling and comments are normalised, so two spellings of one program have one canonical text and therefore one CID. A BeatScript 2 canonical text begins with its version line, #! beatscript 2; a BeatScript 1 canonical text has no #! line, so the first line alone tells the version."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "canonical form"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
