<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Several notes sounded together on one step."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chord term"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ChordTerm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ChordTerm> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A name derived from the bytes it names (a CID): the same content always has the same identifier."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "content identifier"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#modelCID> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "pflow's modelCID is the content identifier of a net model; ProgramCID and NetCID are the same kind of name for a BeatScript program and for the net a deck runs."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ContentId> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The app's text command language: every control is a noun (what) and a verb (do what). One verb, describe, tells a user what a noun can do."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "control language"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#DjConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlLanguage> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLanguage> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A line that sets something about the deck rather than playing notes: tempo, key, a level."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "control line"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ProgramLine> .
