<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A gesture the app carries out for the DJ: a timed change to one or both decks."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "perform move"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#DjConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PerformMove> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhraseTemplate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhraseTemplate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A template that compiles a phrase to a whole track: arrange from template(NAME, PHRASE). The phrase is the vocal line (its syllables the line's length, its stress the accents and the beats, its meter the subdivision); the arrangement is the template's own."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhraseTemplate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "phrase template"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhraseTemplate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhraseTemplate> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Phrasebook> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Phrasebook> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A curated set of phrases a program sings by id: sing @id on melody. The public-domain one is lines of verse, scripture, speech and work song first published before 1929, as a CC0 file with one CID."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Phrasebook> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "phrasebook"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Phrasebook> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Phrasebook> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhrasebookEntry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhrasebookEntry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One line of a phrasebook: its words, the lyric BeatScript sings them as, where and when it was first published, and its meter as a step pattern."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhrasebookEntry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "phrasebook entry"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhrasebookEntry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PhrasebookEntry> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Product> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Something shipped under a name: a website, a language, an app or an MCP server."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "product"@en .
