<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A step that is silent."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "rest"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RestTerm> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RestTerm> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "N places in a cycle, one token circulating, one transition per step; transitions at pulse positions carry a note binding, the rest are silent. Realises a Euclidean rhythm."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Realised as a cycle of places and transitions with one token; the cycle makes it a state machine in pflow's terms."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rhythm ring"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#PetriNet> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#EngineNet> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#PetriNet> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A rhythm ring is a state machine in pflow's sense: every transition has one input place and one output place, and the net holds exactly one token."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RhythmRing> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A set of pitch-class offsets in semitones from a root."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scale"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Scale> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named group of lines that plays as one section of the piece. Unrelated to ns:SongSection, which is a genre-level template slot; a section block is whatever the author wrote."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "section block"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionBlock> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionBlock> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What a section means in one family: which roles play and how much energy it carries."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Section profile"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionProfile> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One numbered place in a song structure, filled by a section."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Section slot"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionSlot> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Segment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Segment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One stretch of a set list: a track or loop and how long it plays."@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Segment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "segment"@en .
<https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#Segment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://beatscript.app/ontology/ns#DjConcept> .
